      "statusChangeID": null,
      "value": "@{5a9fe9983955314156acc4f7|full_name} Although I agree that many users would use this field for alternate uses, rather then the intended purpose, I believe having the official UI suggest alternative uses to the pronouns field might not be suitable in this case. Suggestions of alternate uses might lead to confusion for some users, especially when some cultures will be less aware of the idea of preferred pronouns.\n\nFurthermore, If the official UI states alternate uses for the pronouns field, some users who care about their pronouns might feel uncomfortable.\n\nCurrent industry standard maintain distinct fields for pronouns and pronunciation for the above reasons, and I believe this should be followed for VRChat. I'm not creating a motion to make a pronunciation field, I dont think it's really necessary, but merging pronunciation into the pronouns field might not be a good decision.",
      "viewerReactions": null,
      "voteID": null
    },
